            "review_title": "Review at Izakaya Idaten",
            "review_text": "Mengkysan\nCheltenham, United Kingdom208 contributions\n0\nVery silly ordering system.\nJul 2026 • Family\nLet's start by saying that the issue is not the staff. The staff were friendly and did their job well. The issue is with the stupid ordering system.\nOn entering and being seated, I asked for a beer to drink whilst I looked at the menu but I couldn't have one until I scanned a QR code which revealed a menu and ordering \"system\".\nSo I had to find my beer, add it to a cart and then..... well, I don't know really.\nDo I have to add all my food and order together ? Do I check out the beer in my cart ? Who knows ?\nSo, two hungry kids, a hungry wife and a hungry me didn't really know what to do.\nI saw an item of interest in the menu but wanted to know what it was, so I tapped it and just got the name but almost no info.\nWhat if I wanted it but no mushrooms or no onions ? It seemed very klunky and basic...and confusing.\nI had no clue and the poor waitress could only use Google Translate to help. \nAt this point my beer had somehow arrived but I wanted to leave the restaurant as it was too difficult. \nAll I wanted to do was open a menu, see an item, point at it and have it appear in front of me but this was too difficult.\nHowever, my wife insisted and we somehow got a meal for my son, two very small portions of fries and that was it.\nThe meal we were sure my daughter had ordered never turned up and when we asked, it was confirmed it had never been ordered and so out of 4 people, only 1 ate.\nThis is the owner's fault. It is not the staff; they can only work with the tools they've been given, so this issue is the owner's.\nThe staff were pleasant, tried hard but the language barrier was too great. That said, they could see we were not happy and provided some free puddings as an attempt at damage limitation but damage had been done. We asked for the bill and quickly left.\nSo, I can't recommend this place and until the silly ordering system is removed, I suggest you go elsewhere.\nSorry girls: you tried and I know the language is our problem not yours. It's your country and we are guests but had it been a regular menu, I'm sure we'd have worked it out.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nIf they are still using a QR menu system, don't bother eating there.\nService\nWritten July 20, 2026",
